(242519, 15125, 5313, '<td valign="top">Well, this is the very first time I''ve seen any results for a photo I''ve submitted!  It was so exciting.  Thanks for the votes!<br/> <br/>I must tell you about the photo:<br/> <br/>I''m Canadian but I lived in Northern Ireland for many years married to a fellow from there.  He''s passed away now and the Shillelagh in the photo is his.  (It''s an ancient Irish weapon)  The shovel was made by my father before I was born (probably in the depression days) and represents emptying my ashes from the fireplace each day when we lived over there.  And of course, the shamrock plant I bought in memory of my husband.  Thus the title, "Loving Memories from the Auld Sod".<br/> <br/>This was so much fun!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-03-21 00:37:34.</i></td>', 'Well, this is the very first time I''ve seen any results for a photo I''ve submitted!  It was so exciting.  Thanks for the votes! I must tell you about the photo: I''m Canadian but I lived in Northern Ireland for many years married to a fellow from there.  He''s passed away now and the Shillelagh in the photo is his.  (It''s an ancient Irish weapon)  The shovel was made by my father before I was born (probably in the depression days) and represents emptying my ashes from the fireplace each day when we lived over there.  And of course, the shamrock plant I bought in memory of my husband.  Thus the title, "Loving Memories from the Auld Sod". This was so much fun!', '2003-03-21 00:11:48.000000', '2003-03-21 00:37:34.000000', 0),
